      source: "Engraved portrait of Gerardus Mercator at the age of 62, half-length with dividers and a globe, in an oval inscribed 'Aetatis suae LXII' with a cartouche stating that Frans Hogenberg had the portrait of Gerardi Mercatoris Rupelmundani painted in 1574; Library of Congress Prints and Photographs Division, LCCN 2006675892, an impression illustrated in the 'Atlas sive Cosmographicae meditationes' (Duisburg, 1595), item-level date 1595. The engraver is not named on the Library's record. It is a lifetime portrait dated 1574 and identified by its own inscription. The file is the Library's 3283 x 4096 master scan cropped to the plate and cartouche and downscaled to 900 x 1200 with no upscaling.",
