      source: "Oval portrait photograph of Higuchi Ichiyo captioned in print 'Higuchi Ichiyo shoei (Meiji 28)', that is a portrait of 1895, as reproduced in the Japanese literature anthology 'Gendai Nihon bungaku zenshu, vol. 9' (Kaizosha, 1931; National Diet Library digital collection pid 2627917, whose record carries the library's public-domain mark) and displayed on the National Diet Library's digital exhibition 'Portraits of Modern Japanese Historical Figures', page for Higuchi Ichiyo. The photographer is not named. Rights review: the exhibition's current 'About This Site' page states that all images used in the exhibition are in the public domain and may be reused, including commercially, with the source cited (the library notes that its terms were unchanged when its website policy was updated in February 2025). The basis is also age: the photograph dates from 1895, the sitter died in 1896, and it was reproduced in a Japanese book of 1931, so any Japanese term had expired long before the 1996 US restoration date and the image is in the public domain in the United States. Caveats: the individual photographer and the first publication of the photograph were not found; the image is a halftone reproduction. Identity rests on the printed caption. Cropped from the library's 448 x 495 pixel exhibition image to the oval portrait to remove the caption, 344 x 450 pixels (never upscaled). A larger exhibition image from a 1959 biography was not used because its source book is not openly viewable.",
