      source: "Anonymous drawing of Rifa'a al-Tahtawi in Arab dress, artist and date unknown. The same drawing is printed as plate 3 (captioned 'Rifa'a Bey Rafi' al-Tahtawi') in Jurji Zaydan's Tarajim Mashahir al-Sharq, volume 2, third edition (Cairo: Matba'at al-Hilal, 1922), Internet Archive scan from the Bibliotheca Alexandrina (item AAlexandrina-084569), where the text calls it his portrait; that 1922 print is the verified publication basis. The file is the clearer Wikimedia Commons scan of the same drawing ('Rifa'a el-Tahtawi.png', which its uploader attributes to a 1912 edition of his Manahij al-Albab), converted to JPEG on a white background at its original 758 x 877 pixels, not upscaled.",
